# KEFEN Overview

## Purpose

This document provides a short public overview of KEFEN within the broader WLRT / WaveCounter / BitCapital ecosystem.

It is intended to clarify how KEFEN is currently documented, what kind of role it may play in the evolving architecture, and how it should be understood at the present stage.

## What KEFEN is

KEFEN is documented as a structural and experimental token component within the evolving ecosystem built around WLRT, WaveCounter, and BitCapital.

At the current stage, KEFEN is described primarily in research, methodological, and architectural terms rather than as a conventional financial product.

## Current context

Within the current public documentation structure, KEFEN is positioned as part of a broader architecture that includes:
- WLRT as the theoretical framework;
- WaveCounter as the applied system logic;
- BitCapital as the applied implementation and internal research environment;
- KEFEN as a token-related structural component within this evolving system.

## Functional interpretation

Depending on the relevant document and analytical layer, KEFEN may be described as a utility-oriented, executive-oriented, or structurally assigned token component.

Any such interpretation remains subject to separate definition in policy, architecture, and implementation materials.

## Current limitations of interpretation

At the present stage, public documentation should not interpret KEFEN as:
- equity in BitCapital or any other entity;
- ownership of pool assets or reserves;
- a guaranteed claim on profits, returns, or distributions;
- a finalized legal or governance entitlement unless separately documented.

## Documentation role

The purpose of KEFEN-related public documentation is to provide a stable public reference point for identity, context, architecture, and future documentation layers.

It is not intended to function as a financial promotion document.
